-- title:
--   From HTo G G Hat Half Product Outcome Operator Snoc
-- statement:
--   **The ordered G-hat half-product obeys a snoc recursion.**
--
--   Let `params` have a field model and let `family` be a slice-indexed polynomial family. If $H_n(xs,gs)$ is the ordered product of completed slice effects, then for every $n$, point tuple $xs$, outcome tuple $gs$, $x\in\mathbb{F}_q$, and completed outcome $g$,
--
--   $$
--   H_{n+1}\left(\operatorname{snoc}(xs,x),\operatorname{snoc}(gs,g)\right)=H_n(xs,gs)U_x(g).
--   $$
--
--   Here $U_x(g)$ is the completed slice effect for outcome $g$ at height $x$. The identity exposes the final factor and is used by the reverse-product adjoint lemma.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.fromHToG_gHatHalfProductOutcomeOperator_snoc`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
